The distinction can be written cleanly as follows. A market order accepts the best available price at the moment of execution. A limit order imposes a price ceiling or floor: $\begin{aligned}
\text{buy limit executes when } & P_{\text{ask}} \le \bar P_{\text{buy}}, \\
\text{sell limit executes when } & P_{\text{bid}} \ge \bar P_{\text{sell}}.\end{aligned}$ A limit order may be partially filled if the full quantity is not available at acceptable prices.

